/T (In addition to mean average precision, another metric commonly used for search systems is normalized discounted cumulative gain \(nDCG\), which is more nuanced in that the relevance of documents is not binary \(relevant versus not relevant\) and one document can be labeled as more relevant than another in the test suite and scoring mechanism.)
